<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johann Reinhold Patkul</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1660–1707</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johann Reinhold Patkul was a Livonian nobleman who led the opposition of the Baltic German nobility to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-xi-of-sweden">Charles XI</a>'s reduction of their estates. Sentenced to death in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, he fled and helped build the alliance of Saxony-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> that attacked Sweden in 1700, starting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a>. Handed over to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-xii-of-sweden">Charles XII</a> in 1706, he was executed by breaking on the wheel.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johann-reinhold-patkul.jpg" alt="Johann Reinhold Patkul" width="320" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johann_Patkul.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
